          "derivation": "All six are Latin-via-French derivatives of levis/levāre and are listed together under legwh- by Watkins. leaven < ME levain < OF levain < VL *levāmen 'that which raises' (Klein). lever < OF levier/leveor 'lifter', from lever < levāre. alleviate < LL alleviāre (ad- + levāre). elevate < L ēlevāre (ex- + levāre). relieve < OF relever < L relevāre 'raise again, lighten'. carnival < F carnaval < It. carnevale < Old Pisan carnelevare (see node 5); it entered English c. 1540 and reached 'feasting, revelry in general' by the 1590s.",
